.nh
.TH "AEGIS" "1" "May 2026" "aegis 0.1.0-demo" "Aegis Manual"

.SH NAME
aegis-analyze - Fetch and AST-scan a single package — fallback when the incident DB has no record


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBaegis analyze  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
analyze fetches the package's distribution from the registry, runs the
AST risk scanner over its source, applies the allowlist, and prints
a verdict. Spec is [ecosystem/]name@version. Default ecosystem is npm.

.PP
Examples:
  aegis analyze lodash@4.17.21
  aegis analyze @solana/web3.js@1.95.4
  aegis analyze npm/event-stream@3.3.6


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--evidence\fP[=false]
	include file:line snippets for each detected capability

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for analyze

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	emit a machine-readable JSON object to stdout (suppresses human output)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	enable debug-level structured logging to stderr


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBaegis(1)\fP
